1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,333
Thumping again?! Report them! Report them!

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:04,867
Workouts burn more at night~ So what!

3
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:07,767
After 10 p.m., the standard is stricter.

4
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:09,467
Sir, when did you get in here?!

5
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:10,500
Management office.

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,733
They stomp: report them. I stomp: a workout. Double standard, number one.

7
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:17,267
I'm… Modapman.

8
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:22,967
Case summary. 11:04 p.m., 12th floor.

9
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:25,167
Dad, what's floor noise?

10
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:27,567
When upstairs bowls on top of our heads.

11
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:30,933
Just three rounds. Round one: floor noise.

12
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:34,367
Tonight again… the suspect swung the heel hammer.

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,667
What's a heel hammer?

14
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:38,800
Stomping on your heels. Mine's just everyday living noise.

15
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,133
"Do you, perhaps, bowl at home?" Heh heh… what a writer.

16
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:46,300
Let me share the template in the building group chat. Help yourselves~

17
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:51,400
They walk: a heel hammer. I walk: everyday noise. Double standard, number two.

18
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,767
Tonight, I'm telling them.

19
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:56,367
Oh my, it's the dad from downstairs. Take some tangerines.

20
00:00:56,367 --> 00:01:00,100
Oh… yes… tangerines… thank you… looks delicious…

21
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,367
Dad, what about the letter?

22
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:02,667
…It's a thank-you letter.

23
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:05,733
Rather than going up yourself, tell the management office first.

24
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:06,700
When did you get here?!

25
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:07,767
Management office.

26
00:01:07,767 --> 00:01:13,467
Running, walking, it's all floor noise. And it's stricter at night.

27
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:17,300
Your own noise bothers you less, because you can stop it.

28
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:20,367
Round two: parking across two spaces.

29
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:23,833
Two spaces? Where's your conscience? Click!

30
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:26,700
The Justice Neighbor strikes again~

31
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,100
But your car's in two spaces too.

32
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:32,733
I'm scared of door dings. Everyone parks like this~ So what.

33
00:01:32,733 --> 00:01:33,767
…Who took this?!

34
00:01:33,767 --> 00:01:38,900
They do it: posted online. I do it: preventing door dings. Double standard, number three.

35
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:42,733
If you're scared of door dings, park straight inside one space.

36
00:01:42,733 --> 00:01:46,200
Believing everyone does it too is called the false consensus effect.

37
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,900
False… what?

38
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,833
Round three: delivery boxes.

39
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:52,700
Tape still on! They threw out their conscience too.

40
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:56,233
This is a box tower. Apartment art~

41
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:59,567
Honey, your name is on there in giant letters.

42
00:01:59,567 --> 00:02:01,833
Heh heh… it's… an autograph session.

43
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:06,767
They do it: no conscience. I do it: art. Double standard, number four.

44
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:10,900
Delivery boxes: peel off the tape and the label, fold, then paper bin.

45
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,733
You came out of THERE…?!

46
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:13,733
Management office.

47
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:16,467
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

48
00:02:16,467 --> 00:02:19,767
Their stuff in the hallway: blocking. Mine: just for a sec!

49
00:02:19,767 --> 00:02:23,467
Their grilling: a smell attack. Mine: the smell of happiness!

50
00:02:23,467 --> 00:02:26,367
Their hammering: construction. Mine: one little picture frame!

51
00:02:26,367 --> 00:02:29,800
Double standard: five, six, seven!

52
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,867
Dad, our ceiling is upstairs' floor, right?

53
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,400
Right.

54
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,367
Then our floor is downstairs' ceiling.

55
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,067
…Let's bring tangerines downstairs tomorrow.

56
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,967
Here. Read this.

57
00:02:41,967 --> 00:02:45,267
"Do you, perhaps, bowl at home?" …How RUDE!

58
00:02:45,267 --> 00:02:48,467
Honey… that's the template YOU posted in the group chat.

59
00:02:48,467 --> 00:02:50,567
…Lovely writing, sir.

60
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:55,000
They write it: rude. I write it: a masterpiece. Double standard, number eight.

61
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,633
Unit 1203, your own letter has been returned to sender.

62
00:02:58,633 --> 00:03:02,633
That letter was written by Dad himself. Just a wrong answer.

63
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,500
…Classic Modapman.
